WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.361 --> 00:00:02.831
Oh my God, I'm so thrilled
that you're all here.

00:00:02.831 --> 00:00:04.481
I feel like a lot of the time

00:00:04.481 --> 00:00:08.051
you get to speak to one person
who's involved in a project,

00:00:08.051 --> 00:00:11.351
but not, you know, the whole family

00:00:11.351 --> 00:00:13.091
which you're gonna have
different perspectives,

00:00:13.091 --> 00:00:14.999
which is a lot of what your film's about.

00:00:14.999 --> 00:00:17.501
Family and different perspectives.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:20.171
And I just knew out of the
gate when I was watching it,

00:00:20.171 --> 00:00:22.719
I was like this is someone, it seemed,

00:00:22.719 --> 00:00:26.108
tell me if I'm correct,
very personal for you.

00:00:26.108 --> 00:00:27.341
- That's exactly right.

00:00:27.341 --> 00:00:29.731
Yeah, thank you for saying that.

00:00:29.731 --> 00:00:31.211
So yeah, Finn plays a character

00:00:31.211 --> 00:00:34.211
who is like a rockstar online.

00:00:34.211 --> 00:00:36.491
He has 20,000 followers around the world

00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:38.471
from Belarus to Bangladesh.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.860
And his mom is, she runs a
domestic violence shelter,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.831
and the two of them have
like a clash of culture,

00:00:44.831 --> 00:00:46.451
generation, and values.

00:00:46.451 --> 00:00:49.751
- Okay, Finn, I'm so
excited to talk to you.

00:00:49.751 --> 00:00:53.171
I actually got to hang out
with Millie Bobby Brown.

00:00:53.171 --> 00:00:56.183
She did the show, but I heard recently

00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:59.679
that she was talking about
onscreen kissing with you,

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:03.611
and she was teasing that you were-

00:01:03.611 --> 00:01:04.444
- Lousy?

00:01:04.444 --> 00:01:05.277
- Yeah.

00:01:05.277 --> 00:01:06.110
- [Alisha] Quote-unquote lousy.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.261
- And you guys are like
brother and sister,

00:01:08.261 --> 00:01:11.051
like you, and Noah, and
her have grown up together,

00:01:11.051 --> 00:01:13.241
you have raised each
other in certain ways.

00:01:13.241 --> 00:01:14.074
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.930
- How did you feel
about your family member

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.291
calling you a lousy kisser?

00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:18.401
- Yeah, you know what?

00:01:18.401 --> 00:01:21.740
My first like onscreen
kiss was with Millie,

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.851
and so but I didn't know how to like

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:25.931
approach that in any way.

00:01:25.931 --> 00:01:28.429
There was no, just was like,
you're gonna do this thing

00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:30.420
and at the end of the take
you're gonna kiss her.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.491
And then so I just like, kinda just like

00:01:33.491 --> 00:01:35.356
almost like head butted her.

00:01:35.356 --> 00:01:36.533
And then-

00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:37.974
- That's the romantic way of putting it.

00:01:37.974 --> 00:01:38.807
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:38.807 --> 00:01:40.391
The romantic way of
putting it was that yeah,

00:01:40.391 --> 00:01:41.224
I head butted her.

00:01:41.224 --> 00:01:44.621
- Well, I've had to kiss a
lot of people over the years.

00:01:44.621 --> 00:01:47.801
It's very mechanical and I was excited

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:49.841
'cause I was gonna kiss
my boyfriend, at the time,

00:01:49.841 --> 00:01:51.011
on screen, Luke Wilson.

00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:52.421
And I was like, this is gonna be great.

00:01:52.421 --> 00:01:54.421
And then he kissed me in the scene like,

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:58.581
and I was like I thought
this was gonna be different.

00:01:58.581 --> 00:01:59.582
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:59.582 --> 00:02:01.571
- And I was like, oh, that's so weird.

00:02:01.571 --> 00:02:03.221
He gave me the pursed lips

00:02:03.221 --> 00:02:06.971
- Like, I even give open mouth, you know?

00:02:06.971 --> 00:02:08.861
Okay, well I just had to
talk to you about that

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:09.768
'cause I feel like-

00:02:09.768 --> 00:02:10.601
- It's a weird thing.

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:12.761
- Onscreen kissing is a weird world.

00:02:12.761 --> 00:02:17.761
Okay, Alisha used to write
screenplays based on movies.

00:02:18.207 --> 00:02:19.961
Is this true?

00:02:19.961 --> 00:02:24.341
- Yeah, it's not really impressive at all.

00:02:24.341 --> 00:02:25.511
Oh my god.

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:26.831
- [Drew] Oh my god.

00:02:26.831 --> 00:02:28.260
- [Jesse] Oh my god, that's so sweet.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.895
- Straight from my Insta, wow.

00:02:29.895 --> 00:02:30.728
So basically I was obsessed

00:02:30.728 --> 00:02:33.655
with the "Cheetah Girls"
movie, and apparently...

00:02:33.655 --> 00:02:36.890
(audience applauding)

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.884
Lot of fans.

00:02:37.884 --> 00:02:40.481
They made the movie into a book

00:02:40.481 --> 00:02:42.551
you could buy at Barnes
and Noble and read it

00:02:42.551 --> 00:02:44.081
with pictures in it and stuff.

00:02:44.081 --> 00:02:46.566
Then I took that book
that was already a movie

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.331
and made my own, like wrote it up myself

00:02:49.331 --> 00:02:52.871
and made my own screenplay and
made my friends act it out.

00:02:52.871 --> 00:02:54.281
But it was already a movie.

00:02:54.281 --> 00:02:55.114
It was just so-

00:02:55.114 --> 00:02:56.490
- What is unimpressive about that?

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.261
- I mean, like 'cause it
was already a film and-

00:02:59.261 --> 00:03:01.751
- No. This is so smart.

00:03:01.751 --> 00:03:03.581
- Thank you, Drew.
- That's amazing to me.

00:03:03.581 --> 00:03:04.511
- That's what you were going for, right?

00:03:04.511 --> 00:03:06.116
- That's exactly what I was going for.

00:03:06.116 --> 00:03:06.949
- [Finn] Yeah.

00:03:06.949 --> 00:03:08.801
- All right, so what was it like

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:10.961
to work with Jesse as a director?

00:03:10.961 --> 00:03:12.401
- I loved it.

00:03:12.401 --> 00:03:14.411
I was extremely intimidated at first

00:03:14.411 --> 00:03:15.762
'cause I was fan of you.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.290
- Of course, of course.
- Still am. Not was.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.405
Of course, of course, you knew.

00:03:19.405 --> 00:03:20.877
- I'm like the least intimidating person.

00:03:20.877 --> 00:03:21.710
- Yeah, I know.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:22.626
And then I met you and-

00:03:22.626 --> 00:03:24.851
- If you drew a picture of
the least intimidating person

00:03:24.851 --> 00:03:27.401
who's still a human being, I
think it would look like me.

00:03:27.401 --> 00:03:29.351
- I'm honestly intimidated by all actors.

00:03:29.351 --> 00:03:30.697
I feel like they're, I
mean, you just wanted,

00:03:30.697 --> 00:03:33.131
you meet people, you meet other actors

00:03:33.131 --> 00:03:35.647
and you want to be
challenged and you want to

00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:39.161
just drop into the space
and feel really comfortable,

00:03:39.161 --> 00:03:41.081
and I was just nervous.

00:03:41.081 --> 00:03:42.881
It was like the first
time I'd worked in a year

00:03:42.881 --> 00:03:45.401
'cause this was 2021 January,

00:03:45.401 --> 00:03:47.738
and I'd been like cooped up in a house

00:03:47.738 --> 00:03:50.201
and I was just nervous all around,

00:03:50.201 --> 00:03:51.957
and then Jesse just made
me feel so comfortable

00:03:51.957 --> 00:03:54.137
and was so open to collaborating.

00:03:54.137 --> 00:03:56.831
- Well, you did a wonderful job

00:03:56.831 --> 00:03:59.831
helming and leading this beautiful story

00:03:59.831 --> 00:04:03.251
about humanity, and families,
and what's important

00:04:03.251 --> 00:04:06.551
to do with a life and figure
that out along the way

00:04:06.551 --> 00:04:08.261
and take care of other people.

00:04:08.261 --> 00:04:09.851
'Cause I was like, what
does the title mean?

00:04:09.851 --> 00:04:12.063
And when I saw the film, you get it.

00:04:12.063 --> 00:04:14.772
We have a clip of "When You
Finish Saving The World."

00:04:14.772 --> 00:04:16.571
Let's take a look at it please.

00:04:16.571 --> 00:04:18.871
- You don't have to be
interested in politics.

00:04:19.841 --> 00:04:20.891
- But I am.

00:04:20.891 --> 00:04:21.724
- [Alisha] No, you're not.

00:04:21.724 --> 00:04:24.391
It's obvious, but it's cool.

00:04:24.391 --> 00:04:26.411
- You think I'm stupid?

00:04:26.411 --> 00:04:28.004
- No, no, I didn't say that.

00:04:28.851 --> 00:04:30.791
- {Finn] So can you teach me?

00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:31.634
- About what?

00:04:32.518 --> 00:04:35.014
- I watch you talk about things.

00:04:35.014 --> 00:04:39.431
Like, baked things and you talk about them

00:04:39.431 --> 00:04:40.844
with such passion.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.871
(audience applauding)

00:04:43.871 --> 00:04:44.704
- Yeah, perfect.

00:04:47.458 --> 00:04:51.258
Jesse Eisenberg, Finn
Wolfhard, and Alisha Boe.

00:04:51.258 --> 00:04:52.833
"When You Finish Saving The World"

00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:55.072
is in theaters tomorrow.

00:04:55.072 --> 00:04:58.239
(upbeat bright music)

